course: dictionary
lesson: 14986
title: Replication: making exact copies
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Replication is a noun. It comes from the verb replicate, which means to make a copy. Its meaning depends on the topic: a copy of a page, a repeated experiment, or a cell copying its DNA. Look at the words around it to find out which one is meant.
explain: «The photocopier made a replication of the old map.» The clue is the word map, and the sentence is about making something. Replication means an exact copy. Test it: swap in copy and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Scientists needed replication of the results before they believed them.» The clue is the word results. Here replication means doing the experiment again to see whether you get the same result. If the answer matches each time, we trust it more.
explain: «DNA replication happens before a cell divides.» The clues are DNA and cell. The cell is copying its DNA so that each new cell gets a full set. When you meet a word with a science or biology topic, check the words around it first.
fact: Replication is a noun: one replication, two replications.
fact: «Replication» means making an exact copy of something.
fact: In science, replication means doing an experiment again to see whether you get the same result.
fact: In biology, replication is how cells copy their DNA, and how viruses make copies of themselves.
fact: «Replicate» is the verb: to copy, or to repeat exactly.
exercise: «The photocopier made a replication of the old map.» What does replication mean here? | A map of the ocean | *An exact copy | A torn, folded page
exercise: Why do scientists check the replication of results? | To hide the answer from others | *To see whether the same result happens again | To make the experiment longer
exercise: «DNA replication happens before a cell divides.» In biology, replication means | *Copying DNA | Writing a story about cells | Eating food | Shrinking
test: In «Scientists needed replication of the results», which word is the clue that this is about science? | needed | the | before | *results
test: What is a good check for a new word's meaning? | Guess the longest answer | Skip the whole sentence and never return | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Look only at the first letter
exam: Which phrase is about cells copying themselves? | *DNA replication | Replication of results | An exact replication of a page | Copy of a painting
